Id: ssh030w
Severity: WARN
Category: ssh
Check: check_ssh
Fix: Set LogLevel VERBOSE (or INFO); use DEBUG only while chasing a problem.
References: sshd_config(5); CIS Ubuntu Linux 24.04 LTS Benchmark v2.0.0, 5.1.14 (Ensure sshd LogLevel is configured)
Controls: CIS 4.1, 5.4; NIST AC-17, IA-2; ISO 8.5, 8.20; CE Secure configuration, User access control

LogLevel is DEBUG, DEBUG1, DEBUG2 or DEBUG3. sshd_config(5) says that
logging at a DEBUG level violates the privacy of users and is not
recommended: the log then records the detail of every session, and at
the higher levels fills the disk and the remote log with it. CIS allows
INFO or VERBOSE only. VERBOSE adds the fingerprint of the key each
login used, which an investigation wants; set that, and turn DEBUG on
only while chasing a problem, on a test instance where you can.
